    {
      "id": "CARD-AM-09-concept",
      "conceptId": "C-AM-09",
      "kind": "concept",
      "title": {
        "en": "Frequency modulation and deviation",
        "or": "Frequency modulation ଓ Deviation"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "Frequency modulation, or FM, represents the message through changes in instantaneous carrier frequency rather than through carrier amplitude. An ideal FM signal has constant amplitude. Frequency deviation Delta f is the maximum departure from the carrier frequency. For a sinusoidal message of frequency fm, the modulation index is beta=Delta f/fm. FM generally has multiple sidebands, so its bandwidth is not simply the DSB-SC value 2B. Carson’s rule estimates a useful occupied bandwidth as approximately 2*(Delta f+B), where B is the highest message frequency. This is an engineering approximation, not an exact finite spectral boundary. FM is part of the chapter but not required to execute our selected DSB-SC lab.",
        "or": "Frequency modulation କିମ୍ବା FM ରେ Message ଅନୁସାରେ instantaneous Carrier frequency ବଦଳେ। Ideal FM ର Amplitude ସ୍ଥିର। Carrier frequency ଠାରୁ ସର୍ବାଧିକ ପରିବର୍ତ୍ତନ ହେଉଛି Frequency deviation Delta f। Single-tone message frequency fm ପାଇଁ Modulation index beta=Delta f/fm। FM ରେ ଅନେକ Sideband ଥାଇପାରେ। Carson’s rule ଅନୁସାରେ useful bandwidth ପ୍ରାୟ 2*(Delta f+B), ଯେଉଁଠି B ସର୍ବାଧିକ Message frequency। ଏହା ଏକ approximation, ସମସ୍ତ spectral component ର ନିଖୁତ ସୀମା ନୁହେଁ। FM chapter ରେ ଅଛି, କିନ୍ତୁ DSB-SC lab ପାଇଁ ପୂର୍ବଶର୍ତ୍ତ ନୁହେଁ।"
      },
